;; The modules _imp, marshal and _warnings at importlib's needs (PY6a): importlib's _bootstrap and
;; _bootstrap_external import them at their top. _imp answers for pyi's built-in modules (create_builtin
;; imports one through the runtime's import system) and has no frozen or extension modules; marshal's
;; format (dumps, loads: .pyc files) is the import system family's (PY6), which raises; _warnings has only
;; warn, which calls warnings.warn (the stdlib's warnings then runs its pure _py_warnings).

